#Find the key with the maximum value in a dictionary; 
record={"maths":39,"EE":31,"phy":28}
M=record.values()
print(max(M))
print(max(record, key=record.get))
record.get, finds that "maths" has the highest value (39), and gives you back the key "maths" — not the number.

